'Sets: the tag carries real semantics'
description: from a null-valued mapping to a dedup-by-identity container
- >
  YAML's `!!set` denotes a mapping whose keys have null values. yamlover reinterprets the tag as a
  **set-semantics container**: an element appears at most once, so duplicate memberships — forward and
  forward, forward and reverse (`&…[]`), reverse and reverse — collapse to one, deduplicated by
  target. Like `!!yo` — and unlike the `!!mix` marker — it is not a no-op: it changes behavior.
- >
  `!!set` is the inline spelling of the schema keyword `uniqueItems: true`, which is the route for
  json5p and directory overlays — neither has tags.
